{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R36"],
      "pins": ["R36.1", "R36.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTP", "VOUTN"],
      "observed": "R36 is drawn/valued as 24k in the schematic value field, but its description says 24Ω and its MPN FRC0805J240TSD corresponds to a 24Ω 0805 resistor. The Digikey field is also inconsistent (RMCF0805FT750RCT-ND).",
      "expected": "R36 should be a 24 kΩ resistor as indicated by its value and by its role across VOUTP/VOUTN (PoE signature/bleeder), not a 24 Ω resistor.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"R36\") (value \"24k\") (footprint \"Resistor_SMD:R_0805_2012Metric\") (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±100ppm/℃ ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"R36\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "If the BOM is built from the MPN/description, a 24 Ω resistor is populated across VOUTP/VOUTN. This would defeat the PoE detection signature, prevent the board from being detected/powered over PoE, and could burn out the 0805 resistor under PoE voltage.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear sourcing/value mismatch on R36: the schematic value is 24k, while the description and MPN specify a 24Ω resistor, which would populate the wrong part in the PoE signature/bleeder position."
}

